  ('93823e8e-c6a0-46b4-8311-9a6d92ea5178'::uuid, 'bike-walk-macon', 'Grassroots bicycle and pedestrian advocacy nonprofit serving Macon-Bibb County. It promotes safer, more accessible walking, cycling, and transportation choices through advocacy, education, traffic-calming projects, and community events, including Open Streets Macon and Macon Bike Party. Its work began in 2015 with support from the Knight-funded Emerging City Champions fellowship. Kaylee Pruitt became executive director on May 20, 2026, succeeding founder Rachel Umana.

