Source: https://www.unitedwaycg.org/news/hello-house-opens-brookdale-resource-center', 'Low-barrier overnight shelter program at Brookdale Resource Center in Macon, operated through United Way of Central Georgia.'),
  ('6fd9e44d-cc96-4a37-a916-f3a479eca14d'::uuid, 'highland-hills-baptist-church', 'Baptist congregation in East Macon''s Shirley Hills neighborhood, affiliated with the Cooperative Baptist Fellowship. Caitlin Childers Brown and Ethan Brown serve as co-pastors. Community service includes monthly meal packing for Loaves and Fishes, support for Brookdale and Daybreak, and other local partnerships. Sources: https://www.highlandhillsbaptist.org/who-we-are ; https://www.highlandhillsbaptist.org/our-staff ; https://www.highlandhillsbaptist.org/projects-partners ; https://cbfga.org/churches/ . Verified October 23, 2026.', 'Baptist congregation in Macon’s Shirley Hills neighborhood offering worship, spiritual formation, and community service.'),
  ('4a3641a0-bfa6-412e-9d0e-4ee7df280179'::uuid, 'historic-macon-foundation', 'Macon preservation nonprofit working to strengthen neighborhoods by protecting historic architecture and sharing local history. Programs include neighborhood revitalization, historic-property rehabilitation, preservation consulting, educational programs, a tool library, and the Fading Five endangered-places initiative. The foundation formed in 2003 through the merger of the Middle Georgia Historical Society and Macon Heritage Foundation, with roots dating to 1964. Emily Hopkins is executive director.

Sources: https://historicmacon.org/who-we-are ; https://historicmacon.org/contact

