  ('f30ff10c-a5f4-4c02-916a-76a11999f75d'::uuid, 'loaves-and-fishes-ministry-of-macon', 'Macon nonprofit ministry serving people experiencing poverty, homelessness and housing insecurity. Its Jack Steppe Day Life Center provides food, meals, showers, laundry, casework, prescription assistance and help obtaining identification documents. The ministry traces its origins to two ministries formed in 1967. The published staff roster lists Janet Wright as executive director. Sources: https://www.loavesandfishesministry.org/about-us/ ; https://www.loavesandfishesministry.org/services/ . Recognized among Brookdale Resource Center supporters by Macon-Bibb County: https://www.maconbibb.us/five-years-of-hope-brookdale-resource-center/ . Verified October 23, 2026.', 'Macon nonprofit serving people experiencing poverty and homelessness with food, hygiene facilities, casework, and practical assistance.'),
  ('51e2c996-5ec7-4035-a337-1da56753b8e2'::uuid, 'loaves-and-fishes-ministry-of-macon-board-of-directors', 'Governing board of Loaves and Fishes Ministry of Macon. The ministry''s published roster lists Joel Grist as president, Joy King as vice president, Debra Singleton as secretary, Chloe Napier as past president, and fifteen other directors. Source: https://www.loavesandfishesministry.org/about-us/ (verified October 23, 2026; roster term dates are not stated).', 'Governing board of Loaves and Fishes Ministry of Macon, a nonprofit providing food and practical assistance.'),
  ('4b5b8dab-0159-4930-975f-bcdfb0a8cd30'::uuid, 'macon-arts-alliance', 'Regional arts organization and the designated arts agency for Macon-Bibb County, supporting artists, arts organizations, public art and the Mill Hill arts district.

