  ('84d8c581-35be-4117-b17f-818527c1ad2c'::uuid, 'macon-civic-club', 'Macon civic and social club incorporated in 1959, known for producing an annual Musical Revue at the Grand Opera House to raise money for local charities. Members and spouses organize performances, ticket sales, sponsorships, and production work. Its first revue was staged in 1961. Public filing records identify Macon Civic Club Inc. (EIN 58-2087373) separately from the Macon Civic Club Charitable Association (EIN 58-2087375). Officer affiliations on this profile are dated to their supporting filing records; a current roster has not been verified.

Sources: https://maconcivicclub.com/ ; https://projects.propublica.org/nonprofits/organizations/582087373 ; https://projects.propublica.org/nonprofits/organizations/582087375', 'Macon civic club raising funds for local charities through its annual Musical Revue and volunteer service.'),
