  ('ae4f2331-7872-43fa-99e6-e9883c941b43'::uuid, 'men-about-change', 'Youth mentoring nonprofit supporting young men’s academic achievement, emotional development and self-esteem; a 2026 MVP grant recipient.

Government reference (verified October 23, 2026): https://www.maconbibb.us/mayor-community-foundation-announce-4th-round-of-mvp-grants/', 'Youth mentoring nonprofit supporting young men’s academic achievement, emotional development and self-esteem; a 2026 MVP grant recipient.'),
  ('33f24f5d-a8e3-430f-97b6-ac21639fd0e8'::uuid, 'mercer-university', 'Private nonprofit university based in Macon. County government lists Mercer in its agency directory and identifies it as a Brookdale supporter and partner in the planned Unionville free clinic.

Government reference (verified October 23, 2026): https://www.maconbibb.us/outsideagencies/', 'Private university based in Macon offering undergraduate, graduate, and professional education.'),
  ('6e0b85f8-fa1e-4ebc-a71b-63167c147972'::uuid, 'middle-georgia-community-food-bank', 'Macon-based food bank distributing food through community agencies across 24 Middle Georgia counties.

Government reference (verified October 23, 2026): https://www.maconbibb.us/outsideagencies/', 'Macon-based food bank distributing food through community agencies across 24 Middle Georgia counties.'),
  ('4522d9a0-6f54-4557-aaf7-65c06a211a4f'::uuid, 'middle-georgia-for-choice', 'Grassroots reproductive-rights organization active in Macon and Middle Georgia, also known as Middle Georgia 4 Choice or MG4C. It advocates for nondiscriminatory reproductive healthcare, shares community resources, and participates in civic engagement. Julia Callahan and Mia Robbins-Aguilar are documented co-founders; the group grew out of local organizing following the 2022 Dobbs decision.

Sources: https://linktr.ee/midga4choice ; https://www.aol.com/middle-georgia-abortion-rights-group-144419234.html ; https://www.mercercluster.com/article/2026/03/no-kings-protest-march-2026', 'Middle Georgia grassroots organization advocating for reproductive healthcare access and sharing community resources.'),
  ('e4c31702-846c-4aee-84aa-195894638df6'::uuid, 'middle-georgia-regional-commission', 'Regional governmental planning and service agency serving eleven Middle Georgia counties, including Macon-Bibb. Its services include planning and public administration, economic development and lending, technology, transportation and transit, and the Area Agency on Aging. The governing council establishes policy and, through its Budget, Audit and Personnel Committee, hires the executive director; the executive director hires staff.

The 2026–27 officer list identifies Jenna S. Mashburn as chair, Denese Shinholster as vice chair, Kerry Dunaway as secretary and Executive Director Laura M. Mathis as ex-officio treasurer. Macon-Bibb representatives listed on the council roster are Lester Miller, Valerie Wynn, Carlos McCloud, Wallace Herring and Michelle Parks.

Sources: https://www.middlegeorgiarc.org/about-us/mission-values/ ; https://www.middlegeorgiarc.org/mgrc-council-2/ ; https://www.middlegeorgiarc.org/mgrc-council-2/officers-and-committees/ ; https://www.middlegeorgiarc.org/about-us/staff/', 'Regional public agency providing planning, economic development, transportation, and aging services across eleven Middle Georgia counties.'),
