  ('7e7afc77-75be-43b5-905c-f992b98e4dc3'::uuid, 'mt-zion-baptist-church-upson-county', 'Regional faith-based grant recipient developing a rural food pantry and community center with food distribution, computer access and career-readiness activities. This is distinct from Bibb Mt. Zion Baptist Church.

Government reference (verified October 23, 2026): https://www.maconbibb.us/community-foundation-of-central-georgia-awards-more-than-350000-in-grants-to-21-nonprofits/', 'Upson County Baptist congregation developing a community food pantry, computer access, and career-readiness programs.'),
  ('3856a15e-2a2f-43b0-b3a2-5f4c037dbf6b'::uuid, 'mulberry-outreach-community-garden', 'Mulberry Street United Methodist Church''s volunteer garden, established in 2010 to supply fresh produce to Macon Outreach''s food pantry. It is a church ministry program, not a separate nonprofit. Sources: https://www.mulberrymethodist.org/missions ; https://www.mulberrymethodist.org/serve . Verified October 23, 2026.', 'Mulberry Street United Methodist Church''s volunteer garden, established in 2010 to supply fresh produce to Macon Outreach''s food pantry.'),
  ('61a32251-2a13-4e7a-b2c6-ef7b8592e90f'::uuid, 'mulberry-street-united-methodist-church', 'Historic United Methodist congregation in downtown Macon, established in 1826. Its community ministries include Macon Outreach at Mulberry, which began in 1971, and an outreach garden supporting the ministry''s food pantry. Source: https://www.mulberrymethodist.org/about-us ; https://www.mulberrymethodist.org/missions . Verified October 23, 2026.', 'Downtown Macon United Methodist congregation offering worship, faith formation, and community outreach.'),
  ('9d098a93-57f3-4678-9273-8c80e2698f65'::uuid, 'museum-of-arts-and-sciences', 'Macon museum providing arts and sciences exhibitions, educational programs, a planetarium and natural-history experiences.

Government reference (verified October 23, 2026): https://www.maconbibb.us/outsideagencies/', 'Macon museum providing arts and sciences exhibitions, educational programs, a planetarium and natural-history experiences.'),
  ('b63b1fd8-8a3a-4533-9753-1dcced6473de'::uuid, 'museum-of-aviation-foundation', 'Private charitable foundation supporting aviation preservation and STEM education at the Museum of Aviation near Robins Air Force Base. The foundation states it is not part of the Department of Defense and has no governmental status.

Government reference (verified October 23, 2026): https://www.maconbibb.us/outsideagencies/', 'Private charitable foundation supporting aviation preservation and STEM education at the Museum of Aviation near Robins Air Force Base.'),
  ('93d71ca9-ebc1-436d-abcc-409d87a0354f'::uuid, 'national-cybersecurity-alliance', 'National nonprofit providing public cybersecurity and privacy education. Macon-Bibb County links to its Stay Safe Online resource in the official outside-agencies directory as “NCSA – Stay Safe Online.” This is a national resource, not a Macon-based organization.

Sources: https://www.maconbibb.us/outsideagencies/ ; https://www.staysafeonline.org/aboutus', 'National nonprofit providing public cybersecurity and privacy education.'),
  ('3c595583-9f16-4232-8af6-15eae7b49218'::uuid, 'newtown-loans', 'Community Development Financial Institution led by Lauren Marshall. Provides financing, training and technical assistance for small businesses and real-estate development; NewTown''s staff page identifies a $21 million loan fund.

Source: https://newtownmacon.com/our-work/staff/ (reviewed October 23, 2026).', 'Community Development Financial Institution providing loans, training, and technical assistance for small businesses and real-estate development in Macon.'),
  ('78a347ff-bef3-4f04-933e-1ee0b5dc4dc9'::uuid, 'newtown-macon', 'Independent nonprofit revitalizing downtown Macon through local business and real-estate finance, entrepreneur training, events and trail development. James Fritze is President and CEO; Erin Keller is Chief of Staff and Vice President for Development. Its current staff directory lists twelve staff members. Related programs and bodies include NewTown Loans, Main Street Macon, the Business Improvement District, the Downtown Macon Community Association, the Habersham Downtown Dreams Initiative, and the Ocmulgee Heritage Trail. Knight Foundation is a documented funder.

NewTown staff provide BID management through NewTown Macon BID Management; the district has its own board. The Main Street and BID board rosters are separately recorded with undated-roster caveats. A full current roster of NewTown Macon''s own corporate governing board was not located on the reviewed pages. Josh Rogers appears in a memorial section and is not included as current staff.

Sources (reviewed October 23, 2026): https://newtownmacon.com/our-work/staff/ ; https://newtownmacon.com/experience/bid/ ; https://newtownmacon.com/experience/main-street-macon/ ; https://newtownmacon.com/business-resources/dmca/ ; https://newtownmacon.com/business-resources/downtown-diversity-initiative/ ; https://newtownmacon.com/trails/history-of-the-trail/ ; https://knightfoundation.org/articles/grantee-story/newtown-macon/

Government reference: https://www.maconbibb.us/outsideagencies/', 'Independent nonprofit revitalizing downtown Macon through local business and real-estate finance, entrepreneur training, events and trail development.'),
  ('d11b2901-2486-4fd0-925f-d60d10ec3145'::uuid, 'next-level-community-development-center', 'Community organization named among the 2026 Macon Violence Prevention grant recipients supporting local children and families.

Government reference (verified October 23, 2026): https://www.maconbibb.us/mayor-community-foundation-announce-4th-round-of-mvp-grants/', 'Macon youth organization offering year-round academic support, mentoring, and summer learning through Camp Zion.'),
  ('48ead39e-acba-47d8-bfcd-351a9a3cb45b'::uuid, 'north-central-health-district', 'Georgia Department of Public Health district serving thirteen Central Georgia counties, including Bibb. Its Macon district office coordinates public-health programs and county health departments. The leadership directory lists Kim Cook as district health director and Michael Hokanson as district public information officer.

Source: https://northcentralhealthdistrict.org/about-us/', 'Georgia public-health district coordinating health services and county health departments across thirteen Central Georgia counties.'),
  ('eab7f7a5-ce90-40a9-aa89-4647edba6599'::uuid, 'ocmulgee-heritage-trail', 'Public-private recreational trail partnership. NewTown Macon plans expansions and raises private funds; Macon-Bibb County operates and maintains completed improvements as public park facilities. This record represents the trail initiative, without implying a separate corporation.

Source: https://newtownmacon.com/trails/history-of-the-trail/ (reviewed October 23, 2026).', 'Macon recreational trail initiative connecting communities along the Ocmulgee River through public and private partnerships.'),
  ('0538d7f7-bb98-4ea2-9be8-dfe1b98efa1a'::uuid, 'ocmulgee-heritage-trail-committee', 'Trail committee identified on NewTown Macon''s staff page. Trails Director Mike Ford provides staff support. A full committee roster and its appointment terms were not published on that page.

Source: https://newtownmacon.com/our-work/staff/ (reviewed October 23, 2026).', 'Committee supporting the Ocmulgee Heritage Trail, with staff assistance from NewTown Macon.'),
  ('91b2f2dd-eb34-4937-83a2-22de3e2d203e'::uuid, 'ocmulgee-land-trust', 'Land trust identified in NewTown Macon''s official staff biography for Mike Ford, which states that he has served as its president since July 2011. This source does not establish a parent-subsidiary relationship with NewTown Macon.

Source: https://newtownmacon.com/our-work/staff/ (reviewed October 23, 2026).', 'Macon nonprofit conserving land and easements to protect water quality, wildlife habitat, and the Ocmulgee River basin.'),
  ('1f22a55d-9d44-454f-a390-a05855f7d566'::uuid, 'otis-redding-foundation', 'Macon charitable foundation supporting music education and the philanthropic legacy of Otis Redding; referenced in the county’s 2026 Otis Redding Way dedication announcement.

Government reference (verified October 23, 2026): https://www.maconbibb.us/macon-bibb-to-dedicate-otis-redding-way-in-honor-of-music-legend/', 'Macon foundation supporting music and arts education while preserving Otis Redding’s philanthropic legacy.'),
  ('b632c214-b6b6-41ed-a2c1-b4f14cda949c'::uuid, 'pace-center-for-girls-macon', 'Local girls’ support program of Pace Center for Girls, named among the 2026 Macon Violence Prevention grant recipients.

Government reference (verified October 23, 2026): https://www.maconbibb.us/mayor-community-foundation-announce-4th-round-of-mvp-grants/', 'Macon program supporting girls through education, counseling, advocacy, and services that prevent juvenile-justice involvement.'),
  ('598bcd8c-ff49-436e-b557-3aec715c57d5'::uuid, 'piedmont-macon-medical-center', 'Macon hospital within nonprofit Piedmont Healthcare. County government identifies it as a partner in a 2026 community grief-support event. Formerly Coliseum Medical Centers; Piedmont’s official history records its transition to the nonprofit system in 2021.

Sources: https://www.maconbibb.us/griefsupportsession41626/ ; https://www.piedmont.org/about-piedmont/hospital-leadership/piedmont-macon-medical-center-leadership', 'Piedmont Healthcare hospital providing inpatient, emergency, surgical, and other medical services in Macon.'),
  ('e3ac102d-2ae2-4db3-92f1-680b3044f6f9'::uuid, 'piedmont-macon-north-hospital', 'Macon hospital within nonprofit Piedmont Healthcare. The county’s April 2026 grief-support announcement identifies both Macon hospital campuses as part of Georgia’s largest nonprofit hospital system. Formerly Coliseum Northside Hospital.

Sources: https://www.maconbibb.us/griefsupportsession41626/ ; https://www.piedmont.org/about-piedmont/hospital-leadership/piedmont-macon-north-hospital-leadership', 'Piedmont Healthcare hospital providing emergency, surgical, and other medical services in north Macon.'),
  ('858dc92d-d6c0-43e7-a568-c3696c504f77'::uuid, 'pilot-club-of-jones-county', 'Jones County, Georgia service club in the Middle Georgia area, affiliated with Pilot International and listed in its official Georgia District club directory. Pilot service priorities include brain health and safety, preparing youth for service, and supporting caregivers. The Georgia District''s 2023-24 club-president roster lists Beth Coon; a current club president has not been verified.

Sources: https://www.pilotinternational.org/join/find-a-club/georgia ; https://pilotgeorgia.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/ga-district-club-presidents-2023-24.pdf ; https://pilotgeorgia.org/', 'Jones County service club affiliated with Pilot International, supporting brain health, youth service, and caregivers.'),
  ('3231c0e9-9400-40c1-ad64-3511674b2d99'::uuid, 'pilot-club-of-macon', 'Macon, Georgia service club affiliated with Pilot International and listed in its Georgia District directory. Pilot service priorities include brain health and safety, youth service, and caregiver support. The Macon club has supported therapeutic camp access for people with developmental disabilities and distributed children''s bicycle helmets at Open Streets Macon. The Georgia District''s 2023-24 club-president roster lists Carolyn Glover; a current local president has not been verified.

Sources: https://www.pilotinternational.org/join/find-a-club/georgia ; https://pilotgeorgia.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/ga-district-club-presidents-2023-24.pdf ; https://www.openstreetsmacon.com/pleasanthill ; https://www.41nbc.com/two-developmentally-disabled-individuals-get-chance-to-go-to-summer-camp-for-free/', 'Macon service club affiliated with Pilot International, supporting brain health, youth service, and caregivers.'),
  ('c0f96c32-d12a-4431-86ad-6efe121d6665'::uuid, 're-cycle-macon-ccmi', 'Centenary Community Ministries program providing refurbished bicycles, helmets and locks to people needing reliable transportation. The program accepts referrals from Daybreak, Brookdale, the Salvation Army and River Edge. Source: https://centenarycommunityministries.org/recycle-macon . Verified October 23, 2026.', 'Centenary Community Ministries program providing refurbished bicycles, helmets and locks to people needing reliable transportation.'),
  ('97b264b0-1bd9-4b52-9131-fb079e68a8a2'::uuid, 'rebuilding-macon', 'Macon nonprofit providing home repairs at no cost to low-income homeowners, especially older adults and people with disabilities. Founded in 1992, it coordinates volunteers and community support to improve home safety, accessibility, comfort and energy efficiency. The published staff roster lists Derek Thomas as executive director and Tom Birmingham as construction manager; the board roster is explicitly dated 2025. Sources: https://www.rebuildingmacon.org/mission ; https://www.rebuildingmacon.org/team . Government references: https://www.maconbibb.us/outsideagencies/ ; https://www.maconbibb.us/communitydevelopmentweek2026/ . Verified October 23, 2026.', 'Macon nonprofit providing home repairs at no cost to low-income homeowners, especially older adults and people with disabilities.'),
  ('d26ca9e6-c3c8-4e8d-b724-62576c2ac756'::uuid, 'rebuilding-macon-board-of-directors', 'Governing board of Rebuilding Macon. The organization''s website publishes a roster labeled 2025, listing Bob King as chair, Dan Riley as secretary and nine other members. The site says board terms last three years, begin in January, and may be renewed once. The published roster does not establish who holds office in 2026. Source: https://www.rebuildingmacon.org/team (verified October 23, 2026).', 'Governing board of Rebuilding Macon, a nonprofit providing home repairs for low-income homeowners.'),
  ('5334b46e-9a84-4c67-9767-a78be0ac13f8'::uuid, 'rescue-mission-of-middle-georgia', 'Faith-based nonprofit offering residential life-recovery programs for men, women and children facing addiction, homelessness, domestic violence and other hardships. Its outreach began in 1952, and Macon Rescue Mission, Inc. was chartered in 1956. Pat Chastain is president and CEO. The mission also operates thrift stores and community outreach. In fall 2026, the Community Foundation of Central Georgia awarded $23,000 toward a planned 56-bed men''s transitional home. Sources: https://www.rescuemissionga.com/about-us/ ; https://www.rescuemissionga.com/about-us/leadership/ . Government reference: https://www.maconbibb.us/community-foundation-of-central-georgia-awards-more-than-350000-in-grants-to-21-nonprofits/ . Verified October 23, 2026.', 'Faith-based nonprofit offering residential life-recovery programs for men, women and children facing addiction, homelessness, domestic violence and other hardships.'),
  ('c875bb12-e08c-4c6a-8454-065d1ddf8f9f'::uuid, 'rescue-mission-of-middle-georgia-advisory-board', 'Thirteen advisors listed separately from the mission''s executive board and board of directors. An advisory role does not establish operational or legal oversight. Source: https://www.rescuemissionga.com/about-us/leadership/ (verified October 23, 2026; the roster does not state term dates).', 'Advisory board supporting the Rescue Mission of Middle Georgia, separate from its executive board and directors.'),
  ('b8d9a11b-f71f-4b84-9da1-6494e0fb0796'::uuid, 'rescue-mission-of-middle-georgia-board-of-directors', 'Six directors listed separately from the mission''s executive board. Source: https://www.rescuemissionga.com/about-us/leadership/ (verified October 23, 2026; the roster does not state term dates).', 'Board of directors of the Rescue Mission of Middle Georgia, a nonprofit providing residential recovery programs.'),
  ('27de30b7-e867-44cd-8c2e-66bd25b7c1a4'::uuid, 'rescue-mission-of-middle-georgia-executive-board', 'Six-member executive board, including chair, vice chair, secretary, treasurer and two members at large. Source: https://www.rescuemissionga.com/about-us/leadership/ (verified October 23, 2026; the roster does not state term dates).', 'Executive board of the Rescue Mission of Middle Georgia, with officers and members at large.'),
  ('ae6239d5-e1bf-4439-891f-e5599336bec0'::uuid, 'river-edge-behavioral-health', 'Central Georgia community behavioral-health provider offering mental-health, substance-use recovery, intellectual and developmental disability services, and supportive housing. Its executive directory identifies Cass Hatcher as CEO. The February 2025 GPB article describes its housing and treatment role in Macon''s homelessness-response network.

Sources: https://river-edge.org/about/message-from-the-ceo ; https://river-edge.org/about/executive-leadership-team ; https://www.gpb.org/news/2025/02/14/these-macon-laws-prohibit-homeless-camps-arrests-are-rare-heres-why', 'Central Georgia community behavioral-health provider offering mental-health, substance-use recovery, intellectual and developmental disability services, and supportive housing.'),
  ('5fa13bbd-d3ef-4627-bdaa-a862991c075c'::uuid, 'river-edge-foundation', 'Georgia 501(c)(3) established by River Edge to develop affordable housing and provide supportive services for people experiencing homelessness and disability. Distinct from the public River Edge Behavioral Health community services board.

Government reference (verified October 23, 2026): https://www.maconbibb.us/communitydevelopmentweek2026/', 'River Edge nonprofit developing affordable housing and supportive services for people experiencing homelessness and disabilities.'),
  ('580fbf46-cf6e-432e-b796-8d6e3bfa084b'::uuid, 'ronald-mcdonald-house-macon', 'Macon family lodging program and facility operated by Ronald McDonald House of Central and Southwest Georgia. Provides guest rooms, meals, laundry and shared spaces for families of children receiving medical care. It is a chapter program and facility, not a separate charity. Source: https://ronaldmcdonaldhousecentralswga.org/about-us/our-house/ (verified October 23, 2026).', 'Macon lodging program providing rooms, meals, and practical support for families of children receiving medical care.'),
  ('86f6d9e5-c2a7-4a52-9abc-4f0421fab804'::uuid, 'ronald-mcdonald-house-central-southwest-georgia', 'Regional charitable chapter supporting families whose children need medical care, including lodging, meals and practical support at its Macon Ronald McDonald House. Formerly Ronald McDonald House Charities of Central Georgia, it adopted its current name in October 2026. Patty Gibbs is president and CEO. Sources: https://ronaldmcdonaldhousecentralswga.org/about-us/our-staff/ ; https://ronaldmcdonaldhousecentralswga.org/about-us/our-house/ ; https://middlegeorgiaceo.com/news/2026/10/ronald-mcdonald-house-central-and-southwest-georgia-unveils-new-name-and-brand-identity/ . Government reference: https://www.maconbibb.us/community-foundation-of-central-georgia-awards-more-than-345000-in-grants-to-nonprofits-serving-central-georgia/ . Verified October 23, 2026.', 'Regional charity providing lodging, meals, and practical support for families whose children need medical care.'),
  ('548d5830-8857-486c-9f03-7b63b07f4b8b'::uuid, 'ronald-mcdonald-house-central-southwest-georgia-board', 'Governing board of Ronald McDonald House of Central and Southwest Georgia. The official 2026 roster lists eighteen distinct directors, with Sandy Duke as chair. Chris Snow appears twice on the source page and is recorded once. Source: https://ronaldmcdonaldhousecentralswga.org/about-us/board-of-directors/ (verified October 23, 2026).', 'Governing board of Ronald McDonald House of Central and Southwest Georgia.'),
  ('d4d90fba-8283-430a-9e93-92b34479b045'::uuid, 'salvation-army-central-georgia-housing-homeless-services', 'Local housing and homelessness program of The Salvation Army of Central Georgia. The official local page lists a bridge-housing and clinical-treatment model serving 20 veterans, 42 beds for women and children, and 60 beds for single men. This is a regional ministry program, not a separate nonprofit. Source: https://www.salvationarmyusa.org/usa-southern-territory/georgia/central-georgia/homelessness/ (verified October 23, 2026).', 'Salvation Army program providing shelter, housing support, and related services for people experiencing homelessness in Central Georgia.'),
  ('983e3e0b-88fe-4272-876c-b3d23f7f9ae5'::uuid, 'sleep-in-heavenly-peace-macon-chapter', 'Local chapter of a charitable organization mobilizing volunteers to build and deliver beds to children who do not have one.

Government reference (verified October 23, 2026): https://www.maconbibb.us/community-foundation-of-central-georgia-awards-more-than-350000-in-grants-to-21-nonprofits/', 'Local chapter of a charitable organization mobilizing volunteers to build and deliver beds to children who do not have one.'),
  ('a1224a88-0e9e-418f-974c-242ab2d28316'::uuid, 'society-of-st-andrew-georgia', 'Food-rescue and hunger-relief nonprofit named among Brookdale Resource Center supporters by county government.

Government reference (verified October 23, 2026): https://www.maconbibb.us/five-years-of-hope-brookdale-resource-center/', 'Georgia food-rescue organization mobilizing volunteers to recover surplus produce and distribute it through hunger-relief partners.'),
  ('5ab64fcd-5718-433b-9cf6-8be2395da514'::uuid, 'sonrise-ministries-jones-county', 'Faith-based community ministry in Jones County, also known as Jones County Outreach Center. Its published history names Ronnie Hinson as founder. Reporting documents thrift-store, food, and housing assistance, including New Sonrise Inn.

Sources: https://jonescountyoutreachcenter.wordpress.com/ ; https://middlegatimes.com/g/macon-ga/n/42430/sonrise-ministries-gray-here-help', 'Faith-based community ministry in Jones County, also known as Jones County Outreach Center.'),
  ('9ba8ac69-7d63-4ea6-a0bb-8ec6f562221a'::uuid, 'southern-majority', 'Political communications and consulting firm founded in 2017. Compiled research describes the firm as managing Lester Miller’s 2020 and 2024 mayoral campaigns and receiving payments from his campaigns.

Source: mbresearch/Orgs/Southern_Majority.md and mbresearch/People/Lester_Miller.md. These summarize historical campaign work; this is a client relationship, not a claim that Miller owns or manages the firm.', 'Political consulting and communications firm supporting campaigns, advocacy, and community engagement.'),
  ('858ba39e-447e-4e32-90d4-afc23a970035'::uuid, 'state-court-of-bibb-county', 'County state court. Its current contact directory names Chief Judge Jeff Hanson, Judge Sharell F. Lewis, Interim Clerk Holly Hoyle and Chief Probation Officer Amy Hartley.

